    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d769">

                <pb facs="0726" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002/972: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-01-26T18:00:00+09:00">January 26, 1940—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 27—2:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. Reference Shanghai’s despatch No. 2770, December 21, 1939,<anchor n="43"
                        xml:id="d769-f1"/> taxation of imports and exports by Swatow Rehabilitation
                    Commission: tax on postal parcels entering Swatow.</p>
                <p>My British and French colleagues have informed me recently that they are
                    instructed to make representations to the Foreign Office if and when I am
                    similarly instructed. The Department’s instructions are respectfully
                    requested.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
